{"title":"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Abby, Bridget, and four of their classmates will be seated in two rows of three for a group picture, as shown. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/6/ba6415e404832f3ef2afc016acabd151270a56ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\text{X}&amp;\\quad\\text{X}\\quad&amp;\\text{X} \\\\ \\text{X}&amp;\\quad\\text{X}\\quad&amp;\\text{X}  \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />\nIf the seating positions are assigned randomly, what is the probability that Abby and Bridget are adjacent to each other in the same row or the same column?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62288adf7def381546cf64f1be78f68e4fa0236.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{2}{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{7}{15} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"384\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/39014ba3bceae8e41365f76f8a69fb909c1ed40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 !$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> ways to arrange the kids.\n</p><p>Abby and Bridget can sit in 3 ways if they are adjacent in the same column:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6a775b47b14a21dd93ba1826b1835acc1eb6261.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\text{A}&amp;\\quad\\text{X}\\quad&amp;\\text{X} \\\\ \\text{B}&amp;\\quad\\text{X}\\quad&amp;\\text{X}  \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"103\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20cbec639a1d87c2112358e14ded3ac45d51c4bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\text{X}&amp;\\quad\\text{A}\\quad&amp;\\text{X} \\\\ \\text{X}&amp;\\quad\\text{B}\\quad&amp;\\text{X}  \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c81ff832177c7f08b2664e3865d8554f5bd83c3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\text{X}&amp;\\quad\\text{X}\\quad&amp;\\text{A} \\\\ \\text{X}&amp;\\quad\\text{X}\\quad&amp;\\text{B}  \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"103\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\nFor each of these seat positions, Abby and Bridget can switch seats, and the other 4 people can be arranged in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2da866442e69c040daf44260b4728d37e98de313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways which results in a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/121e294fd18950bf396b9a1fd4674e49b4fc5764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 2 \\times 4!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" /> ways to arrange them. \n</p><p><br />\nBy the same logic, there are 4 ways for Abby and Bridget to be placed if they are adjacent in the same row: they can swap seats, and the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people can be arranged in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2da866442e69c040daf44260b4728d37e98de313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9af99d1dd11fa09f7c9c2cf4a93d9ed4f86f73c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 2 \\times 4!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> ways to arrange them.\n</p><p><br />\nWe sum the 2 possibilities up to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92be7b8cfbf558aae185a9c3aadcdb0677093ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(3\\cdot2)\\cdot4!+(4\\cdot2)\\cdot4!}{6!} = \\frac{14\\cdot4!}{6!}=\\boxed{\\frac{7}{15}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"303\" height=\"48\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>If you got stuck on this problem, refer to AOPS Probability and Combinations.\n</p><p>~Nivaar\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can ignore other students, and treat Abby and Bridget as indistinguishable (since we only care about adjacency, not their order). Thus, the total number of ways is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/890776ba120c6a50fa5524237bf65985345fe41d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(S) = _{6}C_{2} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> .\nIn one row, they can be adjacent 2 ways:  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab965242f9d125d65e4c9b58a1e453f999c0981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 2 rows = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"14\" />. \nIn one column, they can only be adjacent 1 way: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/a/d5a6ab315df649d395be8b6df64406ee661ae334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\cdot 3 cols = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" />. \nAdd these cases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/916792d3166c88332e80557114630afd438626b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+3=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, and therefore, P(Abby and Bridget sitting adjacent) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73e02d89b1e0ebf48e4791328680f41b186c1ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{7}{15}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can split the seating into two separate cases: if Abby is sitting on the corners, and if Abby isn't. If Abby is sitting in the corners, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> chance Bridget is sitting next to Abby, so there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/3/6039e952a9edce5857fd3a94a74dc836f4dc5b90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5} \\cdot \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{4}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" /> chance for the first case. Meanwhile, if Abby is sitting in the middle row, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac40ce1434cda0943c408cc185f5976212d95801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> chance Bridget is sitting next to Abby, so there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef2e58e56e16d1bbcc8f95910cfc02a92f87d2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5} \\cdot \\frac{2}{6} = \\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" /> chance for the second case. Therefore, P(Abby and Bridget are sitting adjacent to each other) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90a387d8328021aa65db592620625a9e0018012d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{15} + \\frac{1}{5} = \\boxed{\\frac{7}{15}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"117\" height=\"49\" /> , or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9b68aaa5462a2128fb5d06e10449ebc58b641f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<pre>~strongstephen\n</pre>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YNH7IwMSsh0\">https://youtu.be/YNH7IwMSsh0</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/EMe9rve8wI0\">https://youtu.be/EMe9rve8wI0</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/sZhsVX4xIgg\">https://youtu.be/sZhsVX4xIgg</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 8\">2018 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2018\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017105616\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 192/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5083/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.304      1 -total\n 57.88%    7.122      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 40.35%    4.964      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16886:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017105616 and revision id 275439. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}